Project Design Phase – Educational Management System

Objective:
To plan and structure the system in a way that ensures smooth development, easy maintenance, and scalability.

⸻

1. Requirement Analysis (Small Steps)
	•	List all functional requirements: admissions, student tracking, staff management, communication.
	•	List non-functional requirements: performance, security, usability, scalability.
	•	Identify users: students, teachers, administrators.
	•	Document inputs, outputs, and workflows for each module.

⸻

2. System Architecture Design
	•	Decide on architecture type: Client-Server / Web-Based / Service-Oriented.
	•	Identify main modules:
	1.	Admissions Module
	2.	Student Progress Module
	3.	Staff Management Module
	4.	Workflow Automation Module
	5.	Communication Module
	6.	Reports & Analytics Module
	•	Define how modules will interact with the database and each other.

⸻

3. Database Design
	•	Identify all necessary tables: Students, Staff, Courses, Attendance, Notifications, Reports.
	•	Define relationships (ER diagram) between tables.
	•	Determine primary keys, foreign keys, and constraints.
	•	Prepare sample data for testing.

⸻

4. User Interface (UI) Design
	•	Create wireframes for each module/page: login, dashboard, admissions form, report view.
	•	Decide layout, navigation flow, and color scheme.
	•	Ensure the UI is user-friendly and responsive.

⸻

5. Workflow & Process Design
	•	Map step-by-step workflows for each module:
	•	Admission request → Approval → Student registration → Notification.
	•	Attendance marking → Progress update → Report generation.
	•	Identify automation opportunities in workflows.
	•	Ensure smooth communication between modules.

⸻

6. Technology Stack Finalization
	•	Backend: ServiceNow platform, Node.js / PHP
	•	Frontend: HTML, CSS, JavaScript
	•	Database: MySQL / PostgreSQL
	•	Tools: Workflow automation, reporting modules, dashboards

⸻

7. Security & Access Design
	•	Define user roles: Admin, Teacher, Student.
	•	Set permissions for each role.
	•	Ensure data privacy (e.g., student grades, staff details).

⸻

8. Prototype / Mockup Creation
	•	Build small prototypes or wireframes for key modules.
	•	Test usability with sample users.
	•	Refine design based on feedback.

⸻

9. Documentation
	•	Document module design, workflows, database schema, and UI wireframes.
	•	Maintain diagrams: ERD, flowcharts, module interaction diagrams.

⸻

10. Design Approval
	•	Review design with project stakeholders / mentors.
	•	Incorporate suggestions and finalize design for development phase.
